course: dictionary
lesson: 14023
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The bike was well maintained, with oiled gears and new brakes.» Maintained means kept in good condition, because the oiled gears and new brakes show that someone looked after it.
explain: «The cyclist maintained a speed of 15 km an hour up the hill.» Here maintained means kept at the same level. The speed did not go up or down. In a maths problem, this tells you the speed stayed the same.
explain: «He maintained that he had never touched the vase.» Here maintained means kept saying something is true, even when others doubt it. The word "that" after it is a clue: it is followed by a statement that someone is sticking to.
fact: Maintained is the past tense of maintain, so it tells you about something that already happened.
fact: «Maintained» can mean kept in good condition, kept at the same level, or kept saying something is true.
fact: «The park is maintained by the council» means the council pays for the park and looks after it.
fact: The noun is maintenance, as in «The bus needs regular maintenance.»
fact: Check the clues: a machine, a speed, or a claim followed by "that" each point to a different meaning.
exercise: «The garden was well maintained, with neat lawns and trimmed hedges.» What does maintained mean here? | Kept saying it was true | *Kept in good condition | Kept at the same speed | Stolen
exercise: «The cyclist maintained a speed of 15 km an hour up the hill.» What does maintained mean here? | Forgot | Hid | Broke | *Kept at the same level
exercise: «He maintained that he had never touched the vase.» What does maintained show? | He broke the vase on purpose | *He kept saying it was true | He paid for the vase | He stopped talking
test: «The council maintained the playground, so the swings were safe.» What does maintained mean here? | Closed it for ever | *Paid for it and looked after it | Measured it | Painted it bright blue
test: In a maths problem, «the train maintained a speed of 80 km an hour.» What does this tell you? | The train was broken | The speed stopped | *The speed stayed the same | The speed went up
exam: Which word is the noun from maintained? | well-maintained | maintained | maintain | *maintenance
